      {
        "type": "text",
        "label": "The brief",
        "body": "How can two brands with different purposes create something that feels entirely their own? The brief explored a care-kit sleeve that connects Sneaker LAB’s product expertise with BSTN’s roots in basketball and streetwear."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "eyebrow": "Creative approach",
        "title": "Thinking Unity",
        "divider": "/assets/projects/superbalist-divider.svg"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "label": "Thinking Unity",
        "body": "Thinking Unity. Rather than placing two identities side by side, the concept finds common ground in the culture surrounding the product. The basketball court provides the organising idea: a graphic language of lines, rhythm, movement and connection."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "label": "The visual direction",
        "body": "Court markings become packaging architecture. Bold monochrome graphics, orange-court studies and a restrained typographic system translate the energy of the game into a sleeve designed for sneaker culture. Presented as a pitch concept, not a released product."
      }
